      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The first school in the area opened in 1808 at John Widner’s home, long before the town was formally established.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Freelandville%2C_Indiana",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Fort Widner was built in 1812 to protect settlers during the second war with Great Britain, marking early frontier defense.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Freelandville%2C_Indiana",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Bethel Church, organized in a log schoolhouse in 1847, remains one of Freelandville’s oldest religious institutions.",
